cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Polissya Wildfire Risk: a dynamic wildfire risk forecasting
  system for the Ukrainian Polissya forest belt
message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sitailo
    given-names: Anhelina
    affiliation: Igor Sikorsky Kyiv Polytechnic Institute
  - family-names: Cherednichenko
    given-names: Artem
    affiliation: Igor Sikorsky Kyiv Polytechnic Institute
abstract: >-
  A day-ahead wildfire risk forecasting system for the Ukrainian
  Polissya forest belt. Ten years of ERA5 reanalysis weather
  (2016-2025) are joined with NASA FIRMS satellite fire detections
  clipped to an OpenStreetMap forest mask. A bidirectional LSTM
  over a 14-day input window reaches ROC-AUC 0.877 and recall 0.922
  on a chronological hold-out set, outperforming logistic
  regression, random forest, and CatBoost baselines. Predictions
  drive a three-tier early warning system with a live inference
  module. Produced under Erasmus+ EcoMinds.
keywords:
  - wildfire
  - fire weather index
  - remote sensing
  - NASA FIRMS
  - LSTM
  - time series
  - environmental monitoring
  - Erasmus+
